  "text": "Duality is a cosmological concept. Writers use the term in two ways. Some treat it as a synonym for dualism. Dualism splits the world into opposing sets. These sets include black and white, light and dark. They also divide male and female. Augustine of Hippo was a famous dualist. In his youth he followed the Persian sage Mani. He later became a Christian bishop. Augustine campaigned against Pelagius. Pelagius taught the “happy heresy.” Augustine saw the physical world as a hindrance. Later Church Fathers kept a dualistic view. Celtic thought did not follow this pattern. Opposites form part of a great whole. They do not stand as enemies.",
